A project-wide bug dating back to Phase 1: every identity was missing publish permission for JetStream ack replies, so ack() had been silently failing server-side since B6/B7 — nats-py's ack doesn't await a response, so it never surfaced as an exception, only in an async error log nothing was checking. Fixed in bootstrap_auth.sh with nsc's --allow-pub-response, applied to every identity, verified live.
BusClient.fetch() raised TimeoutError instead of returning [] when nothing was pending — fixed at the shared jetcore layer so it's not a per-adapter workaround.
