Track F complete — all six steps (F1–F6).

F1 — Seven new JSON Schema files for read/list/delete + the shared FileOperationFailed result (Decision #23), plus a shared decode_path_only_request/PathOnlyRequest in payloads.py since all three request shapes are just {"path"}.

F2–F4 — read_handler.py, list_handler.py, delete_handler.py, each mirroring write_handler.py's structure: resolve_within reused as-is for path safety, security-relevant rejections (traversal/malformed) stay a silent ack+log, "not found" gets a real FileOperationFailed reply. list distinguishes not_found from not_a_directory.

F5 — Found a real, previously-unnoticed gap while wiring this up: no identity in the manifest could actually publish the three new request subjects — webhook-listener-01 only ever published FileWriteRequested, and Phase 3 doesn't build a real front door for the others. Fixed by giving test-observer-01 narrow publish rights for just those three, documented as a deliberate exception to its "read-only observer" framing rather than silent scope creep. __main__.py's run() grew from a 2-way to a 5-way asyncio.gather via a Protocol-typed generic command loop (all four handlers share one shape), so each command gets its own durable consumer per §6's design.

F6 — One test file per handler (happy path, not-found, malformed, traversal — 44 new tests), plus a third entrypoint-level test driving all three new commands through the real 5-way gather sequentially, since read/list/delete run on fully independent consumers with no cross-command ordering guarantee — a concurrent burst would've raced delete against list.

Then verified against the real deployed container, not just automated tests: rebuilt the file-storage-adapter Compose service, created a file through the real Webhook Listener over real HTTP, and drove real read/list/delete commands against the running container from a throwaway script — correct replies, and confirmed the file was genuinely gone from the host bind mount afterward.

160 tests total (up from 116), full suite run 4× clean, ruff/mypy/bandit/pip-audit all clean. This closes out §9 item #1 entirely — the File Storage Adapter now implements its full command set.

