G1–G2 — Scaffold and settings, unremarkable. WebhookSenderSettings is the first adapter to actually use AdapterSettings.subjects at runtime — every prior adapter hardcoded its subscribe subject.

G3 — RelayHandler: single-attempt, best-effort relay (Decision #12), acks regardless of outcome. Verified against a real local HTTP server (a small stdlib-only http.server helper, no mocking — matching this project's ethos throughout), including a case I added once I actually started testing it: a genuine connection-refused (not just an HTTP error status) needs the same "catch and ack" treatment, since Decision #12 doesn't distinguish "server errored" from "server unreachable."

G4 — Entrypoint creates one RelayHandler per configured subject plus a keepalive task (so an empty JETCORE_SUBJECTS doesn't cause immediate exit). Verified with a real running process: real trigger event, real 200 OK logged, real SIGTERM → clean shutdown sequence.

