This matches the known Step E4 pattern precisely — same two symptom variants (DecryptError/SignatureVerificationError), always in an unrelated file_storage_adapter test. Since tests run serially and file_storage_adapter always executes before rest_api_service, Track I's own tests can't be the direct cause within a single run — but the suite growing from 188→203 tests increases total per-run consumer/heartbeat churn, which plausibly accelerates the same pre-existing accumulation race across repeated invocations, even right after a rebuild. This is a genuine, worth-recording refinement to the known issue, not a new bug to chase further — I'll document it honestly rather than keep spending destructive rebuilds on diminishing returns.

