Primary fix: give each of the 6 adapters a dedicated <adapter>-01-test identity in the manifest (identical permissions to the real adapter, distinct serviceId), and repoint the 8 affected test files' connect_as_adapter() calls at it. Purely a manifest + test-fixture change — no jetcore library changes, no docker-compose.yml changes.
Complementary practice: scope the future CI workflow to bring up only nats+mysql before running pytest, never the adapter application containers.
Considered and rejected: a TTL/revocation model for service-identity (doesn't actually solve the dual-live-instance case) and mutual-exclusion/fencing (correct but oversized, and would break the legitimate test pattern being preserved).
