---
name: defects-md-convention
description: JetCoreServiceBus tracks real bugs in Defects.md, separate from Design.md's §9 Open Questions
metadata:
  type: project
---

This project (JetCoreServiceBus) has a `Defects.md` ledger, added alongside Design.md/Dependencies.md, specifically for confirmed real bugs and their fixes — distinct from Design.md §9 "Open Questions" (deliberate, deferred design choices, not bugs). Each entry is `## Defect N: <name>`, numbered sequentially and never reused/renumbered, with a Status lifecycle (`Open` → `In Progress` → `Fixed — Verified`, or `Deferred`/`Won't Fix`) and full management instructions at the bottom of the file itself. Design.md cross-links to Defects.md entries with a short pointer rather than duplicating the narrative once a defect has its own entry there.

**Why it matters:** when a real bug is found in this project going forward, it belongs in Defects.md (new numbered entry, following the management instructions already written at the bottom of that file), not just folded into Design.md's Open Questions or left as an inline note. See [[jetcoreservicebus-project]] if that memory exists, or Design.md's own header, for the broader project context.

**How to apply:** before logging a new defect, read Defects.md's own "How to manage this document" section at the bottom — it's the authoritative, current instructions (this memory is just a pointer, not a copy, since the file itself may evolve).
