All 8 services healthy and stable. Here's the summary:

Defect 1 — Fixed and Verified
The fix: six dedicated <adapter>-01-test identities added to infra/nats/adapter_identities.yaml, each with permissions identical to its real counterpart but a distinct serviceId — so tests can drive real production code paths without ever sharing an identity with a live container.

A real scope correction found while applying it: my original "8 affected files" count (from searching only for connect_as_adapter()) was wrong. Plain connect() calls under a real adapter's serviceId — used throughout every adapter's own handler-level tests and as a "borrowed identity" trigger/replier pattern across adapters — are equally vulnerable to the same collision. The true count was 15 files. All of them, plus every affected conftest.py's fixed durable-name cleanup list, are now updated.

Verification: before the fix, full-suite runs with the container fleet up hit 4-5 failures per 230 tests. After: 6 consecutive clean 230/230 runs, with all 6 adapter containers running the entire time — the exact condition that used to trigger it. ruff, mypy --all-packages, bandit, pip-audit all clean.

One wrinkle along the way, not caused by the fix: the real containers had crash-restarted from genuine JetStream strain during the heavy test load and were stuck in a tight redelivery loop on pre-crash undecryptable messages (768 leftover consumers, 400K+ stream sequence numbers). Cleaned up (purged stream, bulk-deleted stale consumers, reset MySQL binlog) with your approval before re-verifying — didn't do a full infra teardown since you asked for the lighter touch.

A second, distinct issue found while verifying: even with Defect 1 fixed, the real containers' own logs still occasionally show decrypt errors from ordinary test traffic (not identity collision — a cache-propagation timing question). Logged as Defect 2 (Open, root cause not yet isolated) rather than chased further, since it doesn't affect pytest's own results and is out of scope for what you asked me to fix.

Design.md §9 items #5 (now marked fixed) and #7 (new, points to Defect 2), plus the Track K note, are all updated and cross-linked to Defects.md. Saved a project memory noting the Defects.md convention for future sessions.

