Track M (Phase 5) is complete. Here's what actually happened:

M1 — §7.6's table fixed. Replaced the old "preview, not a commitment" placeholder with the real thing, read straight off docker-compose.yml: all 8 services, every env var/port/volume. Found one small honest discrepancy while doing it — JETCORE_LOG_LEVEL is a real, working config option nothing in compose actually sets (defaults to INFO everywhere).

M2 — Demo walkthrough written (README.md § Running the demo): bring-up commands, then the one-request trigger — POST /api/orders?wait=5 — traced through all five things it fans out to (MySQL row, CDC RowChanged, the webhook-relayed file write, HTTP Adapter's outbound call, the sync OrderPersisted reply), every "expected output" block copy-pasted from a real run, not written from memory.

M3 — Executed for real against a clean stack, and this is where it got interesting:

docker compose down -v (wiping DB/JetStream data) → fresh infra/nats/up.sh → hit a real bug: bootstrap_auth.sh's idempotency check intermittently aborted or hung on a rerun, at a different identity each time. Root cause: a 3-stage shell pipe (nsc | yq | grep -q) where grep's early exit on match could SIGPIPE the upstream commands, and pipefail could then report the whole check as "failed" even when it genuinely found the identity. Only became reliably reproducible once the identity manifest grew to 14 entries. Fixed (materialize output before grepping instead of a live pipe), verified with 7 clean reruns, written up in full as Defects.md Defect 4.
Also saw a handful of DecryptError log lines from File Storage Adapter right after a restart — checked the timestamps, confirmed it was a message queued before the restart, exactly the already-known, deliberately-deferred §9 item #4 gap (encryption keypair isn't stable across restarts), not a new bug. Self-resolved after exactly 5 delivery attempts. Noted in README as a heads-up rather than filed as a new defect.
Three real POST /api/orders calls, ./test.sh -q → 235/235 passing.
M4 — added the short "this is a demo, not a deployment guide" disclaimer.

Stack is left healthy and running (just re-verified: all 8 containers up, 235/235 tests passing). Design.md §15 and Defects.md are both updated to match reality, not aspiration.

