Here are the search results for your query about NATS JetStream per-message TTL functionality:

## Key Findings:

**Per-Message TTL Feature Overview:**
Per-Message TTLs have been supported in NATS Server since version 2.11, enabling per-key TTL settings for Key-Value buckets.

**AllowMsgTTL Configuration:**
AllowMsgTTL allows header initiated per-message TTLs. If disabled, then the NATS-TTL header will be ignored. The AllowMsgTTL field can be enabled on existing streams but not disabled.

**Nats-TTL Header:**
To implement per-message TTL, messages can set the "Nats-TTL" header with a duration value. The Nats-TTL header value has a minimum value of 1 second.

**KV Bucket TTL Support:**
KV tombstones can have a TTL to make them expire once not useful anymore, and a stream may have a general MaxAge but some messages may have infinite retention while general keys have TTLs.

**Mirror Stream Limitations:**
When creating a KV mirror, it's impossible to enable per-message TTL support (AllowMsgTTL), even when the source KV bucket has this feature enabled. The SubjectDeleteMarkerTTL setting may not be set on a Mirror Stream.

**Related Feature - Message Scheduling (2.12):**
If you want to use Nats-Schedule-TTL, the stream must also have AllowMsgTTL set to true. It is not automatically enabled by AllowMsgSchedules.


